{## --- Passive-membrane depolarisation field ##}
{% if ctx.elastic_outputs.depolarization is defined %}
{% set dv = ctx.elastic_outputs.depolarization %}
\subsection{Passive-membrane depolarisation $\Delta V$}\label{sec:depolarization}
The conductance-weighted steady-state depolarisation per voxel,
$\Delta V_{\mathrm{passive}} = V_{\mathrm{ss}}(T(\mathbf{x})) - V_{\mathrm{rest}}$, is a cell-type-independent readout: the firing-zone for any spike threshold drops out as the iso-surface $\Delta V = V_{\mathrm{thresh}} - V_{\mathrm{rest}}$ set by the cell substrate (e.g. $\sim$+15\,mV for cortical-pyramidal AIS, $\sim$+8\,mV for fast-spiking interneurons).  Computed analytically from the static-equilibrium tension field with Piezo1 ($\bar{g} = {{ "%.2f" | format(dv.g_piezo1_mS_cm2) }}$\,mS/cm$^2$, $E_{\mathrm{rev}} = 0$\,mV), TREK-1 ($\bar{g} = {{ "%.2f" | format(dv.g_trek1_mS_cm2) }}$\,mS/cm$^2$, $E_{\mathrm{rev}} = -90$\,mV), and the Pospischil cortical leak ($\bar{g}_L = {{ "%.4f" | format(dv.g_leak_mS_cm2) }}$\,mS/cm$^2$, $E_L = {{ "%.1f" | format(dv.E_L_mV) }}$\,mV).  Brain-peak $\Delta V_{\mathrm{passive}} = {{ "%.2f" | format(dv.delta_V_peak_brain_mV) }}$\,mV.

